{
  "suite": "query-operators",
  "description": "The ordinary query operators over one six-row employee fixture: WHERE with =, >, <=, <>, AND and OR; ORDER BY ascending, descending and on two columns with opposite directions; GROUP BY with COUNT, SUM, AVG and MIN/MAX together; LIMIT; and the combinations - WHERE with ORDER BY, WHERE with GROUP BY, GROUP BY with an ORDER BY over the aggregate, and one query using all of WHERE, GROUP BY, ORDER BY and LIMIT at once. The second half is the % (MODULO) binary operator, which was parsed to BinaryOperator.MODULO but never handled in the evaluator's binary-op switch, so a % b threw \"Unsupported binary operator: MODULO\" while the MOD(a,b) function worked: pinned on integers, against MOD itself, on a negative dividend (Snowflake's % takes the sign of the DIVIDEND), on decimals, over a column inside WHERE, and inside a stored procedure's DECLARE. Converted 1:1 from query/QueryOperatorsTest (now retired); the Java asserted row COUNTS and scanned groups with a Java loop and a found-flag, so each converted test pins the whole row set - unordered where the query has no ORDER BY, ordered where it does.",
  "tags": ["query", "converted"],
  "tests": [
    {"name": "where-equals", "steps": [
      {"sql": "CREATE TABLE employees (id INTEGER, name VARCHAR, department VARCHAR, salary INTEGER, age INTEGER)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (1, 'Alice', 'Engineering', 90000, 30)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (2, 'Bob', 'Sales', 70000, 35)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (3, 'Charlie', 'Engineering', 95000, 28)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (4, 'Diana', 'Sales', 75000, 32)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (5, 'Eve', 'Engineering', 85000, 29)"},
      {"sql": "INSERT INTO employees VALUES (6, 'Frank', 'HR', 65000, 40)"},
      {"sql": "SELECT * FROM employees WHERE department = 'Engineering'",
       "expect": {"rows": [[1,"Alice","Engineering",90000,30],[3,"Charlie","Engineering",95000,28],[5,"Eve","Engineering",85000,29]]}}
    ]},
